1
00:00:00,959 --> 00:00:03,169
♪ <i>Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

2
00:00:03,253 --> 00:00:06,798
["Mr. Tailor" playing]

3
00:00:08,508 --> 00:00:10,552
- <i>♪ Fix it</i> ♪
- <i>♪ Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

4
00:00:10,635 --> 00:00:12,846
♪ <i>Holding the scissors</i> ♪

5
00:00:12,929 --> 00:00:16,224
♪ <i>One cut, and it's settled</i> ♪

6
00:00:16,725 --> 00:00:18,643
[security officer, in English]
<i>Do you happen to know this person?</i>

7
00:00:18,727 --> 00:00:20,979
[Dmitri, in English] <i>I have no other way</i>
<i>to contact him.</i>

8
00:00:21,062 --> 00:00:23,314
[in English] <i>I'm very sorry, gentlemen,</i>
<i>but I couldn't help you.</i>

9
00:00:23,398 --> 00:00:24,941
[Samir, in English] <i>You have a lover?</i>

10
00:00:25,024 --> 00:00:28,403
[in English] You give me a try
to make you feel real good.

11
00:00:28,486 --> 00:00:29,612
PREVIOUSLY

12
00:00:29,696 --> 00:00:31,740
You're vulgar!

13
00:00:31,823 --> 00:00:32,699
Cathy?

14
00:00:32,782 --> 00:00:33,742
[in English] Is that…

15
00:00:34,492 --> 00:00:35,535
Karla?

16
00:00:35,618 --> 00:00:38,246
Someone recognized me here,
and I need to avoid them.

17
00:00:38,329 --> 00:00:39,789
Don't leave me. Karla, please.

18
00:00:39,873 --> 00:00:43,418
[in English] …starts at one million pesos.

19
00:00:43,501 --> 00:00:45,628
[in English] One point six million!

20
00:00:45,712 --> 00:00:47,422
This cop seems to have a lot of money.

21
00:00:47,505 --> 00:00:48,840
[in English] One point seven million.

22
00:00:48,923 --> 00:00:53,970
[in English] 2,100,000 pesos.

23
00:00:55,180 --> 00:00:56,097
[in English] Two point five million.

24
00:00:56,181 --> 00:00:58,224
He can have it. It wouldn't fit me anyway.

25
00:00:58,308 --> 00:00:59,851
I won't expose Atoy.

26
00:00:59,934 --> 00:01:01,728
[Dmitri] <i>He's still Janine's father.</i>

27
00:01:01,811 --> 00:01:03,855
[in English] It is best
you stay away from him.

28
00:01:03,938 --> 00:01:05,190
[Karla] <i>Needle on the move.</i>

29
00:01:05,273 --> 00:01:07,609
<i>He received a text message</i>
<i>from someone with a letter B.</i>

30
00:01:07,692 --> 00:01:08,943
I'll take care of Needle.

31
00:01:09,027 --> 00:01:10,737
- [grunts and groans]
- [thumps]

32
00:01:10,820 --> 00:01:12,739
Your boyfriend is rich. Businessman?

33
00:01:12,822 --> 00:01:15,075
No! Police.

34
00:01:15,158 --> 00:01:16,242
Papa Kiko.

35
00:01:16,326 --> 00:01:18,495
[Karla] <i>Boyet is here,</i>
<i>carrying the suitcase.</i>

36
00:01:18,578 --> 00:01:22,874
[Emerson] <i>Boss KM is Kiko Meneses,</i>
<i>not Kevin Martinez.</i>

37
00:01:22,957 --> 00:01:24,501
We're following the wrong needle.

38
00:01:24,584 --> 00:01:26,836
[man] Let go of my boyfriend!
What's the matter with you?!

39
00:01:26,920 --> 00:01:29,380
It's like you're not ready for my arrival.

40
00:01:29,464 --> 00:01:31,716
Am I really your child?

41
00:01:32,217 --> 00:01:33,927
[music fades]

42
00:01:34,010 --> 00:01:35,595
You speak so harshly.

43
00:01:37,514 --> 00:01:39,015
You just got scolded…

44
00:01:40,475 --> 00:01:41,893
and now you're like that?

45
00:01:41,976 --> 00:01:43,561
You're already sulking?

46
00:01:43,645 --> 00:01:47,148
Well, that's what I feel.

47
00:01:48,358 --> 00:01:53,738
- [sobbing]
- [melancholic music playing]

48
00:01:55,240 --> 00:01:57,826
Well, you're wrong!

49
00:01:59,869 --> 00:02:03,540
You know, the reason I do
all of that is because…

50
00:02:03,623 --> 00:02:05,458
I want to make it up to you.

51
00:02:06,751 --> 00:02:09,003
[Olga] I have many shortcomings
when it comes to you, right?

52
00:02:09,587 --> 00:02:13,341
I-I want to give you a good life!

53
00:02:13,424 --> 00:02:14,676
You saw it, Ibyang!

54
00:02:14,759 --> 00:02:17,387
They almost riddled me with bullets!

55
00:02:17,470 --> 00:02:19,347
Right? I tumbled and rolled there!

56
00:02:20,223 --> 00:02:21,850
Because I want to make your life better!

57
00:02:21,933 --> 00:02:23,810
I'll do everything for you!

58
00:02:24,978 --> 00:02:28,940
I'm fine even if we're not rich, Mama.

59
00:02:30,525 --> 00:02:33,862
[Ibyang] But if you're struggling
with your job,

60
00:02:33,945 --> 00:02:36,364
there are other jobs.

61
00:02:37,866 --> 00:02:38,825
[sighs]

62
00:02:38,908 --> 00:02:41,327
This is the only thing I know how to do!

63
00:02:41,411 --> 00:02:46,583
And now, I even have to hustle to pay
for all the damages you caused!

64
00:02:46,666 --> 00:02:48,668
[somber music playing]

65
00:02:52,380 --> 00:02:56,634
Now, you're saying
you're not my child? Huh?

66
00:02:58,094 --> 00:02:59,095
You know, you?

67
00:03:00,221 --> 00:03:01,973
You make me feel bad too.

68
00:03:02,056 --> 00:03:04,934
[music fades]

69
00:03:05,018 --> 00:03:06,978
But do I have time to sulk?

70
00:03:08,730 --> 00:03:10,023
[epic music playing]

71
00:03:10,106 --> 00:03:12,025
I'm sorry, Mama!

72
00:03:12,942 --> 00:03:15,862
[sobbing]

73
00:03:24,662 --> 00:03:29,667
[suave theme music playing]

74
00:03:29,751 --> 00:03:31,586
[motorcycle revving]

75
00:03:31,669 --> 00:03:33,504
[sewing machine whirring]

76
00:03:33,588 --> 00:03:34,464
[scratches]

77
00:03:34,547 --> 00:03:36,049
[snipping]

78
00:03:36,132 --> 00:03:37,967
[clicking]

79
00:03:38,051 --> 00:03:39,385
[sewing machine clacking]

80
00:03:39,469 --> 00:03:41,054
- [gun cocks]
- [gunshots]

81
00:03:41,137 --> 00:03:42,764
[gunshots]

82
00:03:42,847 --> 00:03:45,058
[clicking]

83
00:03:45,141 --> 00:03:47,143
[snipping]

84
00:03:47,227 --> 00:03:49,187
[music swells]

85
00:03:49,270 --> 00:03:52,857
[electronic blipping]

86
00:03:56,527 --> 00:03:58,905
[muffled chattering in the distance]

87
00:03:58,988 --> 00:04:01,241
[suspicious music playing]

88
00:04:10,500 --> 00:04:12,877
Thread 1, can you hear me?

89
00:04:13,753 --> 00:04:16,297
Scissors is carrying the button.
They're now checking in.

90
00:04:16,381 --> 00:04:18,216
[Karla] I repeat. They're checking in.

91
00:04:19,467 --> 00:04:20,426
Thread 1?

92
00:04:22,887 --> 00:04:25,431
Mini Thread? Mini Thread.

93
00:04:27,141 --> 00:04:30,395
[music fades]

94
00:04:30,478 --> 00:04:32,146
[sneaky music playing]

95
00:04:38,069 --> 00:04:40,029
- Karla.
- What, Gavin?

96
00:04:40,113 --> 00:04:41,406
You're giving me a heart attack!

97
00:04:42,865 --> 00:04:46,202
[in English] Heart attack or heartbreak?

98
00:04:46,286 --> 00:04:48,830
Well, both are painful anyway.

99
00:04:49,539 --> 00:04:50,540
I'm sorry.

100
00:04:51,207 --> 00:04:52,625
I'm getting bored here.

101
00:04:52,709 --> 00:04:54,794
Nothing exciting is happening.

102
00:04:55,878 --> 00:04:57,213
What about inside? How is it?

103
00:04:57,297 --> 00:04:59,132
A lot is happening.

104
00:04:59,215 --> 00:05:01,009
Did you see those two men?

105
00:05:01,843 --> 00:05:03,428
[Karla] There, they're the ones
we're chasing.

106
00:05:03,511 --> 00:05:05,221
And that suitcase?

107
00:05:05,305 --> 00:05:08,349
It contains five million pesos,
which we need to get.

108
00:05:10,768 --> 00:05:11,853
[music swells]

109
00:05:14,647 --> 00:05:15,690
- [thumps]
- [grunts]

110
00:05:15,773 --> 00:05:17,025
[in English] Sorry, sorry.

111
00:05:17,108 --> 00:05:19,652
Watch where you're going.

112
00:05:20,445 --> 00:05:22,613
Be thankful I'm in a hurry.

113
00:05:22,697 --> 00:05:23,823
[pensive music playing]

114
00:05:23,906 --> 00:05:26,617
I bumped into that guy earlier.

115
00:05:26,701 --> 00:05:27,994
He seems like a war freak.

116
00:05:28,077 --> 00:05:29,370
I just avoided him.

117
00:05:29,454 --> 00:05:32,707
That's why we need a strategy,
so we don't get into a fight.

118
00:05:32,790 --> 00:05:33,833
How?

119
00:05:33,916 --> 00:05:36,377
[music fades]

120
00:05:40,673 --> 00:05:42,550
[in English] I have a bright idea.

121
00:05:43,593 --> 00:05:45,720
[action music playing]

122
00:05:50,016 --> 00:05:54,020
[music fades]

123
00:05:56,105 --> 00:05:58,149
[clears throat] Uh, boss.

124
00:05:58,733 --> 00:05:59,692
[suspicious music playing]

125
00:05:59,776 --> 00:06:02,570
Boss, I just want to clarify something.

126
00:06:02,653 --> 00:06:03,696
Uh…

127
00:06:06,199 --> 00:06:09,660
We're just friends, okay.

128
00:06:13,623 --> 00:06:14,540
You're crazy!

129
00:06:15,583 --> 00:06:17,543
Of course we'll get a room,

130
00:06:17,627 --> 00:06:19,962
and that's where we'll count the money.

131
00:06:20,046 --> 00:06:21,464
Ah, because it's a couple…

132
00:06:21,547 --> 00:06:23,424
And if there's something missing…

133
00:06:23,508 --> 00:06:26,719
Boss, it's complete.

134
00:06:27,428 --> 00:06:29,722
Remember our deal, boss, it's 10%.

135
00:06:29,806 --> 00:06:30,973
- Okay, okay.
- [smirks]

136
00:06:35,686 --> 00:06:38,231
[music fades]

137
00:06:39,148 --> 00:06:40,566
You're shameless!

138
00:06:40,650 --> 00:06:41,484
[action music playing]

139
00:06:41,567 --> 00:06:42,401
[in English] Sweetheart!

140
00:06:42,485 --> 00:06:43,903
Don't call me sweetheart!

141
00:06:43,986 --> 00:06:45,488
Who are you meeting here?

142
00:06:46,364 --> 00:06:47,448
I'm not meeting anyone.

143
00:06:47,532 --> 00:06:48,699
Actually, this is a surprise for you.

144
00:06:48,783 --> 00:06:51,077
[Gavin] I got a room
so we can have a staycation.

145
00:06:51,160 --> 00:06:52,995
[Karla] Surprise? Where's your friend?

146
00:06:53,079 --> 00:06:54,122
Didn't you say you're with your friend?

147
00:06:54,205 --> 00:06:55,873
Sweetheart, you're the only one I love.

148
00:06:55,957 --> 00:06:57,125
[Gavin] That's just my friend.

149
00:06:57,208 --> 00:06:58,709
[Karla] You're really not honest, huh?

150
00:06:58,793 --> 00:07:01,921
[Cathy, in English] Why would I care
about some couple that I don't even know?

151
00:07:02,004 --> 00:07:02,964
[Karla] You're flirting with her, huh?

152
00:07:03,047 --> 00:07:05,216
I'm not flirting with anyone else!
I'm not like that!

153
00:07:05,299 --> 00:07:07,051
[Gavin] This is just a surprise for you!

154
00:07:07,135 --> 00:07:09,011
That's why I got the room,
to surprise you.

155
00:07:09,095 --> 00:07:10,596
[in English] That's Gavin!

156
00:07:10,680 --> 00:07:12,140
[in English] That's my boyfriend, Mom!

157
00:07:12,223 --> 00:07:13,975
We're having a staycation, right?

158
00:07:15,810 --> 00:07:17,186
[in English] I'm sorry, sweetheart.

159
00:07:18,855 --> 00:07:20,815
I don't want any conflict
between you and my best friend,

160
00:07:21,941 --> 00:07:23,985
that's why sometimes I don't tell you.

161
00:07:24,068 --> 00:07:25,653
[Karla] What if I make you choose, Gavin?

162
00:07:25,736 --> 00:07:26,779
Who will you choose?

163
00:07:27,280 --> 00:07:29,240
Your best friend or your girlfriend?

164
00:07:29,323 --> 00:07:30,950
[tense music playing]

165
00:07:33,995 --> 00:07:35,872
[Cathy, in English] Hey!
What's going on here?

166
00:07:35,955 --> 00:07:38,249
Why are people saying you're a couple?

167
00:07:39,208 --> 00:07:41,502
You told me you went with Jason
to Batangas.

168
00:07:41,586 --> 00:07:42,879
[in English] Let me explain. Okay?

169
00:07:44,005 --> 00:07:46,632
The thing I hate most is being deceived!

170
00:07:47,758 --> 00:07:48,926
[in English] And you!

171
00:07:49,010 --> 00:07:50,761
Is that why you're defending
Gavin so much,

172
00:07:50,845 --> 00:07:52,513
because you're his side chick?

173
00:07:52,597 --> 00:07:53,681
I'm not a side chick!

174
00:07:53,764 --> 00:07:55,600
I'm not that kind of person, Cathy!

175
00:07:55,683 --> 00:07:56,934
You're acting all innocent.

176
00:07:57,018 --> 00:07:58,394
[in English] So, do you have feelings
for Gavin or not?

177
00:07:58,478 --> 00:08:00,730
- Enough!
- [in English] Oh, you're defending her.

178
00:08:01,731 --> 00:08:02,857
Let's talk outside.

179
00:08:02,940 --> 00:08:05,401
No! I'm not going with you!

180
00:08:05,485 --> 00:08:07,945
Oh! Wait.

181
00:08:08,029 --> 00:08:10,031
You know, you're not funny anymore.

182
00:08:10,114 --> 00:08:12,325
- You're causing trouble!
- [in English] Stop it!

183
00:08:12,408 --> 00:08:13,367
[in English] That's my daughter!

184
00:08:14,452 --> 00:08:15,286
You…

185
00:08:15,369 --> 00:08:16,579
[squeals]

186
00:08:16,662 --> 00:08:18,080
- You too!
- [shrieks]

187
00:08:18,164 --> 00:08:20,291
- [gasps]
- [shrieks]

188
00:08:20,374 --> 00:08:21,292
Let go of me!

189
00:08:22,001 --> 00:08:22,960
[grunting]

190
00:08:23,544 --> 00:08:24,670
Let go of me!

191
00:08:24,754 --> 00:08:26,214
Hey. Aren't you a cop?

192
00:08:26,297 --> 00:08:27,548
[Karla] Stop them!

193
00:08:27,632 --> 00:08:29,008
What are you doing?!

194
00:08:29,884 --> 00:08:31,010
[Cathy's mom, in English] Call security!

195
00:08:31,093 --> 00:08:33,137
Gavin! Stop them, oh!

196
00:08:33,221 --> 00:08:34,388
[indistinct shout]

197
00:08:34,472 --> 00:08:35,473
[Karla] Stop them! Gavin!

198
00:08:35,556 --> 00:08:36,557
[Boyet] Let go of me!

199
00:08:36,641 --> 00:08:37,683
[clamoring]

200
00:08:37,767 --> 00:08:38,809
- [Karla] You're with him, right?
- [Cathy's mom, in English] Security!

201
00:08:38,893 --> 00:08:40,561
What are you doing?

202
00:08:40,645 --> 00:08:42,188
[Karla] You're so stupid, huh?

203
00:08:42,271 --> 00:08:43,648
- [Boyet] I said let go of me!
- [clamoring]

204
00:08:43,731 --> 00:08:45,399
I've been looking for you!

205
00:08:45,483 --> 00:08:47,068
You know, I told you to go out, right?

206
00:08:47,151 --> 00:08:47,985
Wait outside…

207
00:08:48,069 --> 00:08:48,986
Sir, that's enough!

208
00:08:49,070 --> 00:08:50,112
That's enough!

209
00:08:50,196 --> 00:08:52,323
- Now, you're speechless?
- Is that it?

210
00:08:53,032 --> 00:08:54,700
You know what? Whatever!

211
00:08:54,784 --> 00:08:57,495
[in English] Gavin. Gavin, I'm sorry.

212
00:08:59,413 --> 00:09:01,290
I'm okay now, Karla. Go.

213
00:09:04,669 --> 00:09:07,171
[in English] So, Gavin, what?
Tell me the truth.

214
00:09:07,255 --> 00:09:09,090
[in English] What's going on
between both of you?

215
00:09:09,799 --> 00:09:11,717
Let's just talk outside. Please?

216
00:09:17,598 --> 00:09:18,599
Fine.

217
00:09:18,683 --> 00:09:19,850
[suspicious music playing]

218
00:09:19,934 --> 00:09:22,478
Excuse me? That's my luggage!

219
00:09:25,231 --> 00:09:26,190
What?

220
00:09:26,274 --> 00:09:27,567
This is mine.

221
00:09:28,234 --> 00:09:30,570
Here, look! The number on my stub.

222
00:09:31,279 --> 00:09:33,823
[tense music playing]

223
00:09:33,906 --> 00:09:35,074
[in English] That's mine!

224
00:09:36,200 --> 00:09:37,535
Let's open this.

225
00:09:52,508 --> 00:09:54,010
Let's go, let's go.

226
00:09:54,093 --> 00:09:54,927
Emerson!

227
00:09:55,011 --> 00:09:56,470
Where have you been? You took so long!

228
00:09:56,554 --> 00:09:58,598
Well, you know, that lady there

229
00:09:58,681 --> 00:10:01,142
asked me to make
a whole pitcher of iced tea.

230
00:10:01,225 --> 00:10:03,227
Let's go. Let's go ahead.
She might catch me.

231
00:10:03,311 --> 00:10:05,605
- Come on, come on.
- Yes, and Boyet might notice

232
00:10:05,688 --> 00:10:07,231
that he has the wrong suitcase.

233
00:10:07,315 --> 00:10:09,483
- Oh?
- Wait.

234
00:10:10,026 --> 00:10:11,152
Where's Gavin?

235
00:10:11,235 --> 00:10:12,653
He's with Cathy.

236
00:10:12,737 --> 00:10:13,863
Cathy's here?!

237
00:10:13,946 --> 00:10:15,740
It's a long story, brother. Later.

238
00:10:15,823 --> 00:10:17,116
- Come on. I'll tell you later.
- [Paldo] Let's go.

239
00:10:17,199 --> 00:10:19,160
- They might catch up to us here!
- Oh, hurry, hurry.

240
00:10:19,243 --> 00:10:20,578
[in English] Sorry, sorry,
sorry, sorry, sorry.

241
00:10:20,661 --> 00:10:21,912
[Emerson] The key, the key.

242
00:10:22,663 --> 00:10:24,123
Where's my money?

243
00:10:24,206 --> 00:10:25,958
[music fades]

244
00:10:26,042 --> 00:10:27,043
Where's my money?

245
00:10:28,127 --> 00:10:29,003
Boss…

246
00:10:29,086 --> 00:10:30,379
[tense music playing]

247
00:10:30,463 --> 00:10:31,839
Boss, we have it!

248
00:10:33,591 --> 00:10:36,302
You can't fool me, you animal.
You're trying to trick me?

249
00:10:36,886 --> 00:10:38,929
You did this to get my money!

250
00:10:39,430 --> 00:10:40,514
Where's the money?

251
00:10:40,598 --> 00:10:42,016
No, boss.

252
00:10:42,099 --> 00:10:44,310
If I was going to take your money,

253
00:10:44,393 --> 00:10:47,396
- why would I meet you here?
- I'll kill you.

254
00:10:47,480 --> 00:10:49,815
- I'll kill you, remember that.
- Boss, I do have the five million.

255
00:10:49,899 --> 00:10:50,941
Hands up!

256
00:10:51,025 --> 00:10:51,859
[music fades]

257
00:10:51,942 --> 00:10:53,027
Both of you!

258
00:10:53,611 --> 00:10:54,445
I'm a cop!

259
00:10:54,945 --> 00:10:57,365
We'll take you to the station.
Explain yourselves there!

260
00:10:58,282 --> 00:10:59,116
Why me?

261
00:10:59,700 --> 00:11:00,660
Arrest him!

262
00:11:00,743 --> 00:11:03,579
He's-- He's the one
who ordered me to steal!

263
00:11:03,663 --> 00:11:06,248
No, both of you,
explain yourselves at the station!

264
00:11:06,332 --> 00:11:09,460
[tense music playing]

265
00:11:14,632 --> 00:11:17,343
[all] Yes!

266
00:11:17,426 --> 00:11:20,221
- Five million pesos-pesos-pesos!
- Oh, wow!

267
00:11:20,304 --> 00:11:23,224
At least now, we can return this
to the rightful owner.

268
00:11:23,307 --> 00:11:24,683
Sis Ame is amazing!

269
00:11:24,767 --> 00:11:27,228
Your idea of switching the suitcases
was brilliant.

270
00:11:27,311 --> 00:11:29,021
- [Emerson] You're right.
- [Karla] Ah, you're awesome.

271
00:11:29,105 --> 00:11:31,690
And Gavin's diversion idea

272
00:11:31,774 --> 00:11:32,983
was also clever.

273
00:11:33,067 --> 00:11:34,735
But Gavin got into trouble.

274
00:11:34,819 --> 00:11:37,321
Boyet punched him,
and then he fought with Cathy.

275
00:11:37,405 --> 00:11:39,281
Well, you didn't intend
for that to happen.

276
00:11:39,365 --> 00:11:41,742
And besides, he insisted
on coming with us, right?

277
00:11:42,326 --> 00:11:44,161
Even so. I allowed it, didn't I?

278
00:11:44,245 --> 00:11:46,122
[gentle music playing]

279
00:11:46,205 --> 00:11:47,957
Oh, oh, where are you going?

280
00:11:48,040 --> 00:11:49,458
I'll look for Gavin.

281
00:11:50,292 --> 00:11:52,002
I'll help him explain to Cathy.

282
00:11:52,086 --> 00:11:54,004
That's the least I can do for him.

283
00:12:00,302 --> 00:12:02,138
Karla will be okay.

284
00:12:02,221 --> 00:12:03,848
First love really is different.

285
00:12:05,057 --> 00:12:06,517
[in English] Gavin, you lied to me!

286
00:12:07,017 --> 00:12:08,978
You told me you went
to Batangas with Jason!

287
00:12:09,061 --> 00:12:11,397
[in English] And then, I find you here
with that… that girl?!

288
00:12:11,480 --> 00:12:13,441
[in English] I'm sorry. Okay?

289
00:12:13,524 --> 00:12:14,942
I just didn't want Karla
to become an issue,

290
00:12:15,025 --> 00:12:16,986
so I didn't tell you she was with me.

291
00:12:17,069 --> 00:12:19,363
- [in English] But we were just--
- [in English] Just what? Huh?

292
00:12:19,447 --> 00:12:21,449
[in English] Acting like a couple
at a hotel?!

293
00:12:21,532 --> 00:12:22,950
[in English] It's not like that.

294
00:12:23,033 --> 00:12:24,493
[in English] Then what's it like, Gavin?

295
00:12:24,577 --> 00:12:27,079
[in English] Gavin,
tell me exactly what's going on!

296
00:12:27,163 --> 00:12:28,205
[somber music playing]

297
00:12:28,289 --> 00:12:30,666
We were helping a friend.

298
00:12:30,749 --> 00:12:32,168
[Gavin, in English] Okay? Karla and I…

299
00:12:32,251 --> 00:12:35,129
We pretended to be a couple
fighting to help that friend.

300
00:12:35,212 --> 00:12:37,214
That was our distraction tactic.

301
00:12:37,298 --> 00:12:39,508
- Do you get it?
- What kind of distraction?!

302
00:12:39,592 --> 00:12:40,843
What kind of help is that?

303
00:12:40,926 --> 00:12:42,136
[Cathy, in English] Gavin,
I don't believe you!

304
00:12:43,679 --> 00:12:44,597
Cathy.

305
00:12:44,680 --> 00:12:45,973
- Karla.
- Wow!

306
00:12:46,557 --> 00:12:49,101
You really came back! The audacity!

307
00:12:49,768 --> 00:12:52,605
I came back because I don't want you
and Gavin to break up,

308
00:12:52,688 --> 00:12:54,231
since I only asked him for help.

309
00:12:55,065 --> 00:12:57,401
Our being a couple earlier
was totally just acting,

310
00:12:57,485 --> 00:12:58,527
even the fight scene.

311
00:12:59,111 --> 00:13:01,405
[gentle music playing]

312
00:13:01,489 --> 00:13:03,365
Gavin is faithful to you,

313
00:13:04,074 --> 00:13:06,243
and you have nothing
to worry about with me.

314
00:13:07,411 --> 00:13:08,662
We're really just friends.

315
00:13:11,040 --> 00:13:14,084
Would Gavin even look for someone else
if you're his girlfriend?

316
00:13:19,507 --> 00:13:20,758
[in English] Okay, fine.

317
00:13:22,051 --> 00:13:24,428
But this is the last time
this will happen.

318
00:13:25,179 --> 00:13:26,013
[in English] Promise.

319
00:13:41,862 --> 00:13:43,155
[music fades]

320
00:13:43,239 --> 00:13:44,490
[in English] Hello, master!

321
00:13:44,573 --> 00:13:45,783
[Atoy on phone, in English] <i>Oh, hello?</i>

322
00:13:46,450 --> 00:13:48,994
How was your first mission?

323
00:13:49,078 --> 00:13:50,704
[in English] Success, master!

324
00:13:50,788 --> 00:13:52,623
- [in English] Success!
- [in English] Master!

325
00:13:52,706 --> 00:13:56,001
You know, we got the package
without the target knowing?

326
00:13:56,085 --> 00:13:57,545
- Isn't that great?
- [Emerson, in English] Mm, yes!

327
00:13:57,628 --> 00:14:00,673
[in English] Very good. Proud of you.

328
00:14:01,549 --> 00:14:03,425
[Ame on the phone, in English]
<i>Oh, we really worked together, Atoy.</i>

329
00:14:03,509 --> 00:14:05,344
There was just a small hiccup at first,

330
00:14:05,427 --> 00:14:08,973
but Karla and I quickly found a way
to switch the suitcase!

331
00:14:10,474 --> 00:14:12,017
Karla?!

332
00:14:12,101 --> 00:14:15,312
[tense music playing]

333
00:14:15,396 --> 00:14:16,438
What-- [clears throat]

334
00:14:16,522 --> 00:14:18,649
Uh, no, uh…

335
00:14:18,732 --> 00:14:20,317
We really lacked manpower.

336
00:14:20,401 --> 00:14:23,529
That's why we needed Karla.

337
00:14:24,113 --> 00:14:25,823
You should have found someone else.

338
00:14:25,906 --> 00:14:28,826
I told you.
I told you to never bring her along.

339
00:14:28,909 --> 00:14:31,620
Something might happen to that girl.

340
00:14:32,204 --> 00:14:33,539
Well, um…

341
00:14:33,622 --> 00:14:38,043
You know Karla,
she's not "just-just", Atoy.

342
00:14:38,127 --> 00:14:39,044
What do you mean "just-just"?

343
00:14:39,128 --> 00:14:40,629
"Just-just", she's not ordinary.

344
00:14:40,713 --> 00:14:41,922
No, no, no, she…

345
00:14:42,006 --> 00:14:43,215
Oh, Atoy, she's like you.

346
00:14:43,299 --> 00:14:44,842
Your sister is just as tough.

347
00:14:44,925 --> 00:14:46,135
Mmm-mmm, mmm.

348
00:14:46,218 --> 00:14:48,053
[mid-tempo rock music playing]

349
00:14:49,346 --> 00:14:50,556
Sister?

350
00:14:50,639 --> 00:14:51,807
[music fades]

351
00:14:51,891 --> 00:14:52,766
Why? Are they siblings?

352
00:14:53,392 --> 00:14:54,602
- [hushes]
- You're too loud.

353
00:14:54,685 --> 00:14:56,353
Eh, ah… [clears throat]

354
00:14:56,437 --> 00:14:57,605
Uh, yes, Atoy.

355
00:14:57,688 --> 00:15:00,357
But the important thing is
we got the five million.

356
00:15:00,441 --> 00:15:02,735
Our mission was successful.

357
00:15:02,818 --> 00:15:04,069
Yes, Atoy.

358
00:15:04,820 --> 00:15:06,697
[action music playing]

359
00:15:06,780 --> 00:15:09,909
We thought this money
would never be returned to us.

360
00:15:09,992 --> 00:15:12,995
Meneses and Boyet,
whom he ordered to steal,

361
00:15:13,078 --> 00:15:14,705
are already in jail.

362
00:15:14,788 --> 00:15:17,166
We also filed a case against them.

363
00:15:17,875 --> 00:15:21,629
The construction of the school in Zambales
will finally begin in a month.

364
00:15:22,212 --> 00:15:26,300
[Odette] Many children in remote areas
will benefit from that school.

365
00:15:26,383 --> 00:15:29,386
We owe you so much. Thank you.

366
00:15:30,012 --> 00:15:31,472
Oh, it's nothing.

367
00:15:31,555 --> 00:15:34,850
We really just wanted to help.

368
00:15:36,810 --> 00:15:38,103
You're amazing.

369
00:15:38,187 --> 00:15:41,482
If we know anyone else who needs help,

370
00:15:41,565 --> 00:15:44,318
- we'll refer them here.
- [Kurt] Hey. Oh, yes!

371
00:15:44,401 --> 00:15:45,611
[in English] Spread the word!

372
00:15:45,694 --> 00:15:48,322
The Children of the Thread
are here to stay!

373
00:15:48,405 --> 00:15:49,531
[Ame] Oh my. [giggles]

374
00:15:49,615 --> 00:15:51,867
- Spread the word, really?
- [Kurt] Hmm.

375
00:15:51,951 --> 00:15:54,203
Sir, please accept this.

376
00:15:54,286 --> 00:15:56,330
- [Emerson] Huh?
- Uh, it's just a small thing.

377
00:15:56,413 --> 00:15:58,582
The staff pooled together for this.

378
00:15:58,666 --> 00:16:01,085
It's less than 10,000 actually. Sorry.

379
00:16:01,669 --> 00:16:03,337
Oh? No, it's not necessary.

380
00:16:03,420 --> 00:16:05,339
You even went to the trouble, and…

381
00:16:05,422 --> 00:16:06,423
This?

382
00:16:07,174 --> 00:16:10,469
I can't… I can't have this.

383
00:16:11,053 --> 00:16:12,846
I don't eat laing.

384
00:16:12,930 --> 00:16:15,140
- Because I'm allergic.
- [both] Ah, laing!

385
00:16:15,224 --> 00:16:18,102
[Emerson] Yes, no. And also, um…

386
00:16:18,769 --> 00:16:20,396
I wish you hadn't gone to the trouble

387
00:16:20,479 --> 00:16:22,231
because we really just wanted to help.

388
00:16:22,898 --> 00:16:26,944
And it's also the first time
we've ever done this.

389
00:16:27,528 --> 00:16:29,571
So, you have a free trial.

390
00:16:29,655 --> 00:16:31,156
- [everyone chuckles]
- You're our first.

391
00:16:31,240 --> 00:16:33,075
Please, accept it.

392
00:16:33,158 --> 00:16:35,619
The amount you returned to us is so big,

393
00:16:35,703 --> 00:16:37,788
for the children too.

394
00:16:38,372 --> 00:16:39,832
It would be easier to accept
if it were cooked.

395
00:16:39,915 --> 00:16:40,916
Oh, just kidding. Just kidding.

396
00:16:41,000 --> 00:16:42,001
Just kidding, just kidding.

397
00:16:42,084 --> 00:16:44,461
We'll go ahead now. Thank you very much.

398
00:16:44,545 --> 00:16:46,296
- All right. We'll go ahead.
- [Emerson] Okay, okay.

399
00:16:46,380 --> 00:16:49,717
- [Kurt] Take care.
- [Emerson] Take care. Take care, okay.

400
00:16:50,342 --> 00:16:51,552
[in English] Bye-bye.

401
00:16:51,635 --> 00:16:52,928
[sneaky music playing]

402
00:16:53,012 --> 00:16:55,556
- Hey, it's like…
- Hmm.

403
00:16:56,056 --> 00:16:57,808
- This feels good.
- It's amazing, right?

404
00:16:57,891 --> 00:16:59,184
Those are good items.

405
00:16:59,268 --> 00:17:02,896
Now I know how Atoy felt.

406
00:17:02,980 --> 00:17:06,775
It really feels good to help, right?

407
00:17:06,859 --> 00:17:11,113
Honestly, Boss E,
even if you didn't do much

408
00:17:11,196 --> 00:17:13,699
in our first mission,
except make iced tea?

409
00:17:13,782 --> 00:17:15,325
[Emerson] Wow!

410
00:17:15,409 --> 00:17:16,785
- [giggles]
- No!

411
00:17:16,869 --> 00:17:20,581
The Children of the Thread
wouldn't exist without you.

412
00:17:21,290 --> 00:17:23,417
So, for the success

413
00:17:23,500 --> 00:17:25,878
of Operation Suitcase!

414
00:17:25,961 --> 00:17:28,797
- [all, in English] Cheers!
- [in English] Hey, cheers! Cheers, cheers!

415
00:17:29,381 --> 00:17:30,924
[giggles]

416
00:17:31,008 --> 00:17:33,635
- [lively chattering]
- [light music playing]

417
00:17:33,719 --> 00:17:35,679
[crickets chirping in the distance]

418
00:17:37,222 --> 00:17:40,476
[melancholic music playing]

419
00:17:40,559 --> 00:17:41,852
[Dmitri, in English] <i>Promise me, child.</i>

420
00:17:42,436 --> 00:17:43,812
You'll stay away from Atoy.

421
00:17:43,896 --> 00:17:46,356
That's what I've been doing, Dad.

422
00:17:47,274 --> 00:17:49,026
That's why Janine and I are leaving.

423
00:17:50,360 --> 00:17:52,321
We're just waiting for her US visa.

424
00:17:52,404 --> 00:17:55,741
[in English] It is best
you stay away from him.

425
00:18:03,123 --> 00:18:05,209
Why does it feel like we're not moving?

426
00:18:05,292 --> 00:18:06,460
Yes, I noticed too.

427
00:18:08,253 --> 00:18:11,048
Well, because you're rowing that way.

428
00:18:11,131 --> 00:18:12,091
I'm rowing this way.

429
00:18:12,174 --> 00:18:14,259
- [Atoy] Well, I thought…
- We really won't move.

430
00:18:14,343 --> 00:18:16,303
- Hello?
- Well, isn't that where we're going?

431
00:18:16,386 --> 00:18:19,681
[chuckling]

432
00:18:47,793 --> 00:18:51,130
[music fades]

433
00:18:53,465 --> 00:18:57,219
[crickets chirping in the distance]

434
00:18:57,302 --> 00:19:00,347
[phone ringing]

435
00:19:02,391 --> 00:19:03,308
Audrey?

436
00:19:04,184 --> 00:19:06,186
[gentle music playing]

437
00:19:06,812 --> 00:19:08,397
Audrey, are you there?

438
00:19:08,480 --> 00:19:13,152
The people at the Zahran embassy
are looking for you,

439
00:19:13,235 --> 00:19:14,403
Samir and his men.

440
00:19:15,320 --> 00:19:18,782
They have an AI-generated photo
of your face.

441
00:19:19,783 --> 00:19:20,742
So, be careful.

442
00:19:22,286 --> 00:19:24,288
Thank you for… for the warning.

443
00:19:25,372 --> 00:19:27,291
Ah, and you, how are you?

444
00:19:28,750 --> 00:19:32,421
[in English] This isn't
a social call, Atoy.

445
00:19:34,214 --> 00:19:36,133
Let's not exchange pleasantries.

446
00:19:37,718 --> 00:19:39,052
[in English] I have to go.

447
00:19:39,136 --> 00:19:40,596
Audrey, wait.

448
00:19:42,514 --> 00:19:43,891
[Atoy on the phone] <i>Audrey…</i>

449
00:19:45,684 --> 00:19:46,643
I still love you.

450
00:19:47,436 --> 00:19:49,271
[melancholic music playing]

451
00:19:49,354 --> 00:19:50,814
You and Janine.

452
00:19:54,026 --> 00:19:55,110
[Atoy on the phone] <i>And, ah…</i>

453
00:19:57,321 --> 00:19:58,363
I know you still love me.

454
00:20:01,200 --> 00:20:03,368
[Atoy] <i>You even called me to warn me.</i>

455
00:20:03,452 --> 00:20:04,536
Thank you for--

456
00:20:04,620 --> 00:20:06,371
[line beeping]

457
00:20:06,455 --> 00:20:07,915
- Audrey?
- [line beeping]

458
00:20:09,541 --> 00:20:11,335
[music fades]

459
00:20:13,629 --> 00:20:17,174
[melancholic music playing]

460
00:20:24,348 --> 00:20:27,976
[sobbing]

461
00:20:42,991 --> 00:20:43,951
[sobbing]

462
00:20:52,209 --> 00:20:54,211
[in English] Please, please. Please.

463
00:20:58,757 --> 00:21:01,009
[in English] Please, please.

464
00:21:01,677 --> 00:21:02,761
[in English] Please.

465
00:21:03,553 --> 00:21:06,139
[Ame on phone] <i>There,</i>
<i>we recovered the suitcase!</i>

466
00:21:06,223 --> 00:21:09,309
The school construction
will now push through.

467
00:21:09,393 --> 00:21:12,729
Our first mission was successful!

468
00:21:14,064 --> 00:21:15,524
Yay.

469
00:21:15,607 --> 00:21:18,193
Oh? Why are you sad?

470
00:21:18,860 --> 00:21:21,446
Is it because
you weren't part of the mission?

471
00:21:22,155 --> 00:21:25,450
Well, Tatoy forbade you, remember?

472
00:21:26,118 --> 00:21:27,286
Because…

473
00:21:29,538 --> 00:21:33,166
I really miss you and Tatoy, Sis Ame.

474
00:21:34,626 --> 00:21:36,378
Hey, Ibyang, what happened?

475
00:21:37,254 --> 00:21:40,465
Mama Olga scolded me.

476
00:21:41,133 --> 00:21:44,469
Because I broke something.

477
00:21:45,721 --> 00:21:49,725
And now she must pay
a huge amount to the owner.

478
00:21:50,517 --> 00:21:53,979
[Ibyang on phone] <i>I didn't</i>
<i>mean to, Sis Ame.</i>

479
00:21:54,604 --> 00:21:57,190
[sobs] I thought

480
00:21:57,774 --> 00:21:59,735
she was in danger.

481
00:22:00,694 --> 00:22:04,197
I thought I was saving her.

482
00:22:05,365 --> 00:22:06,533
But…

483
00:22:07,784 --> 00:22:10,954
I just added to her headache.

484
00:22:11,913 --> 00:22:13,915
Ibyang, don't say that.

485
00:22:15,208 --> 00:22:18,462
Of course, it's natural for your mom
to get angry with you,

486
00:22:18,545 --> 00:22:21,048
because she's just human too.

487
00:22:21,131 --> 00:22:23,675
She's led by emotions,

488
00:22:24,176 --> 00:22:26,011
but she's also a mother.

489
00:22:26,803 --> 00:22:29,765
She'll be angry now, nag you all day,

490
00:22:29,848 --> 00:22:31,933
but tomorrow, everything will be fine.

491
00:22:32,017 --> 00:22:34,269
Really, Sis Ame?

492
00:22:35,687 --> 00:22:39,941
I'm just afraid she'll give me away

493
00:22:40,025 --> 00:22:41,985
if she doesn't want me anymore.

494
00:22:42,569 --> 00:22:44,613
Ibyang, she won't do that.

495
00:22:45,113 --> 00:22:47,908
She searched for you
for a long time, didn't she?

496
00:22:48,867 --> 00:22:51,203
Mama Olga loves you very much.

497
00:22:52,454 --> 00:22:55,207
Just show her that

498
00:22:55,290 --> 00:22:57,501
you're sorry. Make it up to her.

499
00:22:58,085 --> 00:23:00,420
Then everything will be okay.

500
00:23:01,046 --> 00:23:03,215
[sighs] Don't cry anymore, okay?

501
00:23:07,260 --> 00:23:09,971
Olga, the child has only been
with you for a week,

502
00:23:10,055 --> 00:23:12,516
and you're already asking
for next month's pay?

503
00:23:12,599 --> 00:23:15,811
Well, I understand that, madam.

504
00:23:16,478 --> 00:23:19,523
I was just hoping maybe

505
00:23:19,606 --> 00:23:21,191
you could help me.

506
00:23:22,150 --> 00:23:25,112
Maybe it could be included
in the miscellaneous fees?

507
00:23:25,195 --> 00:23:27,197
[scoffs, in English]
It's your fault anyway.

508
00:23:27,781 --> 00:23:29,074
You left her.

509
00:23:29,157 --> 00:23:29,991
If you hadn't done that,

510
00:23:30,075 --> 00:23:31,952
she wouldn't have followed you
to your workplace.

511
00:23:32,536 --> 00:23:34,371
[sighs]

512
00:23:34,454 --> 00:23:37,541
[in English] Just do your job well,
and I may consider giving you a bonus.

513
00:23:37,624 --> 00:23:39,584
Well, there you go, madam.

514
00:23:39,668 --> 00:23:41,336
That would be a big help.

515
00:23:41,878 --> 00:23:45,841
Um, what are the plans for the child?

516
00:23:46,800 --> 00:23:47,926
Don't concern yourself with that.

517
00:23:48,009 --> 00:23:49,719
[suspicious music playing]

518
00:23:49,803 --> 00:23:51,972
Sir, you're there.

519
00:23:52,055 --> 00:23:54,850
Yes, I've been here.
I heard what you said to my wife.

520
00:23:55,600 --> 00:23:57,394
Be thankful she didn't hang up on you.

521
00:23:57,477 --> 00:23:58,895
Do what we agreed on.

522
00:23:58,979 --> 00:24:00,814
That's your only job. Okay?

523
00:24:00,897 --> 00:24:05,318
[line beeping]

524
00:24:06,236 --> 00:24:08,238
[music fades]

525
00:24:08,321 --> 00:24:09,823
"Do what we agreed on.

526
00:24:09,906 --> 00:24:11,408
That's your only job."

527
00:24:12,868 --> 00:24:14,161
[sighs]

528
00:24:15,495 --> 00:24:17,330
So grumpy.

529
00:24:21,751 --> 00:24:24,588
[pensive music playing]

530
00:24:28,383 --> 00:24:32,345
[sneaky music playing]

531
00:24:50,488 --> 00:24:52,991
[phone ringing]

532
00:24:56,745 --> 00:24:59,206
Hello. Friend?

533
00:25:00,415 --> 00:25:02,876
I thought of something
we could make money from.

534
00:25:03,376 --> 00:25:04,836
It's big money.

535
00:25:04,920 --> 00:25:08,965
[music swells]

536
00:25:09,049 --> 00:25:11,092
[electronic blipping]

537
00:25:12,385 --> 00:25:16,806
[tense music playing]

538
00:25:19,184 --> 00:25:22,312
Don't be swayed
by his cuteness and smiles at you,

539
00:25:22,395 --> 00:25:23,730
even if he's your friend.

540
00:25:23,813 --> 00:25:25,273
[Cita] He's a Regalia.

541
00:25:25,357 --> 00:25:28,485
And in the end,
he will still choose his family.

542
00:25:28,568 --> 00:25:30,320
- [Red, in English] <i>How's Janine?</i>
- [Audrey] <i>Still crying.</i>

543
00:25:30,403 --> 00:25:32,989
She said she suddenly remembered
the one who wanted to kidnap her.

544
00:25:33,740 --> 00:25:34,658
[Audrey] Tell me.

545
00:25:34,741 --> 00:25:38,036
Do you know the man
who wanted to take my daughter?

546
00:25:38,119 --> 00:25:40,080
I was accused of being
an accomplice of that

547
00:25:40,163 --> 00:25:41,539
female scammer.

548
00:25:41,623 --> 00:25:42,916
[Olga] Ibyang?

549
00:25:42,999 --> 00:25:45,627
Oh. Something like that.
She looks like her.

550
00:25:46,253 --> 00:25:48,129
UP NEXT

551
00:25:49,214 --> 00:25:51,049
What are you doing out here?

552
00:25:51,132 --> 00:25:52,842
Come on. Get inside the car.

553
00:25:52,926 --> 00:25:54,886
I won't go with you.

554
00:25:54,970 --> 00:25:56,179
Why?

555
00:25:56,263 --> 00:25:57,639
You're a liar!

556
00:25:58,932 --> 00:26:00,558
It's impossible you're my mother.

557
00:26:01,351 --> 00:26:02,394
You're a scammer!

558
00:26:02,477 --> 00:26:04,187
♪ <i>Holding the scissors</i> ♪

559
00:26:04,271 --> 00:26:07,691
♪ <i>One cut, and it's settled</i> ♪

560
00:26:07,774 --> 00:26:09,109
♪ <i>Fix it</i> ♪

561
00:26:09,192 --> 00:26:10,694
Subtitle translation by: Rachel C. Arias
